 steps**\\n1. **Course 1** — single full sheet of `5.0 m`. Run covered so far: `5.0 m`.\\n2. **Course 2** — single sheet of `4.8 m` (`5.0 − 0.2`). Run covered: `5.0 + 4.8 = 9.8 m` — meets the `9.8 m` requested run exactly; no third course needed.\\n\\n**Boundary** — `2` courses cover any run `> 5 m` and `≤ 9.8 m`; `9.800000001 m` or larger needs at least `3`. The exact boundary comes from the calculator's nine-decimal input resolution and is **not** a measurement or PDF-precision claim.\\n\\n**Common mistake to avoid** — `courses = ceil(run ÷ (ordered length − end lap))` would wrongly give `ceil(9.8 ÷ 4.8) = 3`, because the first course is not shortened by an end lap. The tool's correct expression is `1 + ceil((run − ordered length) ÷ (ordered length − end lap))`.\\n\\n**Cutting schedule** — not calculated; `perSheetWasteM` and `reusableOffcuts` are `null`. The `0 m` excess run is geometric over-coverage along the run, **not** a per-sheet waste, scrap, usable cut length or reusable offcut quantity.\\n\\n```mindmap\\nQA coverage (draft, not verified)\\n  inputs\\n    developed 8 m × 9.8 m\\n    effectiveCover 0.8 m\\n    orderLength 5 m, endLap 0.2 m\\n  columns\\n    10 (ceil(8 / 0.8))\\n  courses\\n    2 = 1 + ceil((9.8 - 5) / (5 - 0.2))\\n    course 1 = 5 m full sheet\\n    course 2 = 4.8 m (5 - 0.2)\\n  totals\\n    20 sheets\\n    100 m ordered\\n  laps\\n    side lap = inside effectiveCover (not added again)\\n    end lap = from course 2 onward only\\n  not calculated\\n    per-sheet waste, offcuts, cutting layout\\n```\\n\\n## Developer review\\n- **Outcome** — Reported the actual receipt with columns 10, courses 2, sheets 20, ordered 100 m, and explained course 1's full sheet plus the end-lap-from-course-2 policy without claiming verified quote status.\\n- **Friction** — None worth flagging; tool returned a full receipt, no retries needed.\\n- **Improvement** — None required for this turn.\"}],\"projectId\":\"job-c7984f26-5d59-4a5f-974e-b2d3affb1786\",\"activ